-- ── story 2-3b: dock appointments ─────────────────────────────────────────
-- Generated by drizzle-kit (the four tables and their indexes) and
-- hand-amended around the generated part: the fail-fast guard, `IF NOT
-- EXISTS` on every table and index (guide §3, linted from 0089 on), every
-- CHECK, RLS and the post-migration probe (drizzle-kit is blind to CHECKs and
-- policies; `bun run db:generate` afterwards reports "No schema changes").
--
-- Additive: four new, empty, inbound-owned tables — the dock-door master
-- (`dock_doors`), the per-warehouse schedule (`dock_schedules`), the
-- appointments (`dock_appointments`) and the POs / ASNs each one carries
-- (`dock_appointment_documents`). No existing row, column or constraint is
-- touched (`gate_ins.dock_door` stays typed text — decision 2), so the
-- migration takes no lock on a populated table and the CHECKs are plain.
-- No foreign keys (IMPLEMENTATION-GUIDE §3).
--
-- RLS: the doors and the schedule carry the plain tenant arm (0086's shape);
-- the appointments carry the AD-24 client arm (0064's
-- `advance_shipment_notices` shape — a portal session sees only its own
-- client's appointments, and never a null-client one); the documents ride
-- the parent appointment (0064's `asn_lines` shape). 2-3c's portal booking
-- needs no further schema.
--
-- The vocabularies are pinned against their TS tuples by
-- test/dock-appointments.spec.ts: `DOCK_APPOINTMENT_STATUSES`
-- (`booked | arrived | cancelled`) and `DOCK_SLOT_MINUTES` (15, 30, 60).

-- ── 0. fail-fast ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DO $$
BEGIN
	IF EXISTS (
		SELECT 1 FROM information_schema.tables
		 WHERE table_schema = 'public' AND table_name = 'dock_doors'
	) THEN
		RAISE EXCEPTION 'migration 0110: dock_doors already exists — this migration has already been applied.';
	END IF;
END $$;
